(FUN-24 — a parameter or return type may be `value`, and its runtime tag
 travels with its payload across the call: `describe` dispatches on
 `is a <type>` inside the callee and reaches a different branch for each
 of a number, a text and a float passed through the same slot; `forward`
 takes a value and returns it as a value, and the tag survives the round
 trip (the text still prints as text on the far side).
 (The `value` type itself is mapped in docs/ledger/values.md; this row is
 only the claim that a value crosses a CALL boundary intact.)
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox FUN-24.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   number
   text
   decimal
   round trip
)
To describe with a value called item.
  If item is a number, print "number".
  Otherwise if item is a text, print "text".
  Otherwise print "decimal".

To forward with a value called item. Return a value, item.

describe of 1.
describe of "two".
describe of 3.5.
a value called 'came back' is forward of "round trip".
Print 'came back'.
